// BIDI_N0_DEVIATIONS is how many of the cases above libfribidi ordered
// differently from ICU — all of them rule N0, where fribidi's backward
// scan for the preceding strong context runs past the start of the
// isolating run sequence instead of stopping at sos. palmy follows the
// rule as written, so on these it matches ICU and not fribidi.
BIDI_N0_DEVIATIONS :: 3

// BIDI_LEVEL_CONFLICTS is how many cases the two oracles ordered
// identically while reporting levels neither minimisation nor agreement
// explains. palmy is compared with ICU's ordering on these and with
// nobody's levels.
BIDI_LEVEL_CONFLICTS :: 1

// BIDI_LEVEL_SIMPLIFICATIONS is how many cases the two oracles ordered
// identically while reporting different levels, which is ICU reporting the
// smallest levels that give that order. Conformance clause C1 only
// requires the order, so this is a difference of report, not of result.
BIDI_LEVEL_SIMPLIFICATIONS :: 204

// BIDI_FRIBIDI_CLASSES is fribidi's whole Bidi_Class table, as
// "<lo> <hi> <class>" ranges. palmy's table is generated from Python's
// unicodedata and Perl's unicore files, so this is a third source for the
// same property, and the test walks every one of the 1,114,112 codepoints.
BIDI_FRIBIDI_CLASSES :: `
